      "created_at": "2021-03-04T09:29:35Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-04T09:29:35Z",
      "body": "> Note that I don't know if this bug applies to internally and/or externally created tabs\r\n\r\nNow that you mention it, one of the times this happened to me it was definitely from an external link. I don't remember if the other times were external or internal links.\r\n\r\n> However, I do have a workaround for this bug. That is, when I want to share a newly created tab, in fact any tab, I manually change to the tab above it (as per the tab list) then back to the previous tab (the tab I want to share).\r\n\r\nThanks for this, it worked for me. To add on to this, this still worked for me if you change tabs by swiping on the url bar, which makes the process slightly less annoying and quicker than opening up the tab list (though still annoying). Just mentioning this for the people who had forgotten about the swipe to change tabs feature, like I had :)",
